name sat-11-duel-qra-1
timeout 520
time 1991-01-19T08:00:00Z
wx fixture wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb

# MEASURING RIG, NOT A CAMPAIGN RUNG. `sat-*` files belong to no `.fbc`, are named by no campaign and
# move no doctrine. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md; the criteria: doc/doctrine-evolution.md 4.2.
#
# WHAT IS NEW AGAINST `sat-08-ident-qra`, WHICH THIS FILE IS THE FLIGHT-IDENTICAL TWIN OF: BOTH SIDES
# ARE GRADED. `sat-08` gives its four MiG-29 one `survive until 300` each, and their outcome class is
# then (12, 4) on EVERY allele of their whole strategy space — a constant, and a search cannot climb a
# constant. That is E-30. This file gives the MiG-29 a rung ladder of their own, re-derives the QRA's
# ladders against the current binary, and changes no coordinate, no store and no brief.
#
# THE ADDITION COSTS NO PHYSICS, MEASURED: an `objective` is read by the judge and by nobody else
# (`core/FBZone.h` is RESTRICTED, `FBMissionMonitor` holds its own plan copy), so against `sat-08` under
# the same binary ALL 18 telemetry files are BYTE-IDENTICAL by SHA-256 and the duration is 520.0 s in
# both. What changes is the VERDICT: the four MiG-29 go SUCCESS -> TIMEOUT, i.e. red's V drops 12 -> 8
# and its M becomes a count instead of a constant.
#
# THE MARGIN, IN THE HEAD, AS A NUMBER, ONCE PER SIDE. Every graded quantity here is a PLANAR MIN-RANGE
# between two named units; every rung sits in a MEASURED gap of its own quantity's lever spectrum, and
# every gap is quoted against the chaos amplitude of THAT quantity over the +-3 m spawn grid, taken as
# the WORSE of the two perturbations (one's own and the opponent's) because a rung must survive either.
#
#   RED  narrowest 13.2x — `mg3`'s min-range to `qa2`, 51.9 m against a chaos amplitude of 3.94 m.
#        Widest 22.4x. Four ladders, 18 rungs, one per MiG-29, each against ONE named QRA fighter.
#   BLUE narrowest 10.0x — `qa1`'s min-range to `mg1`, 39.9 m against 3.99 m. The other three run
#        12.4 / 16.4 / 41.3x. Four ladders, 23 rungs.
#
# AND A SECOND CONDITION ON EVERY BLUE RUNG: it must clear the chaos band of its own quantity under
# EVERY DECLARED OPPONENT, not only the committed one. `sat-08`'s inherited ladders obeyed `E18`'s
# one-opponent rule and blue's own class still flipped **3 of 8** under `red sort-near`, `red sort-none`
# and `red sort-right` — a different red allele moves blue's min-range onto a rung that keeps 10x
# against the committed MiG. The rungs here are placed outside [min - 10c, max + 10c] of blue's own S7
# population for all ten red alleles, which is X-17 carried from the SCREEN into the PLACEMENT, and the
# screen then comes back 0 of 8 on all ten pairs.
#
# TWO OF THE FOUR PAIRINGS ARE MUTUAL — `qa1`<->`mg1` and `qa2`<->`mg3` name each other — so on those
# two the same planar range is read from both seats, one asking whether it was closed and the other
# whether it was held open. That is the geometric form of "who holds the cylinder and who breaks it",
# and it is the reason this cell is not two independent one-sided rigs sharing a file.
#
# WHAT REMOVES THE COIN, unchanged from `sat-08`: the four contacts are UNARMED An-26 transports, the
# QRA flies `brief_master_arm sim` and so does the MiG-29 element, so NOBODY CAN BE SHOT. [MESS] 0
# `damage KILL`, 0 `monitor KO`, every `survive` met on every lever of both sides. The engagement that
# decides the sort runs in full; only its lethality is gone.
#
# GENE FAMILIES, MEASURED (tools/fb_duel_arena.py, `--elev const`):
#   BLUE, 24 levers of tools/levers-campaign-g5.txt: BASELINE (14, 15), 10 distinct classes, modal
#     share 60.0 % (15 of 25), S7 0 of 8 on all ten (cell, red) pairs. 10 movers of 24.
#     live  G1 shape 5 of 6, G5 emcon 2 of 3, G3 net 1 of 2, G7 ccip 1 of 2, G6 bias 1 of 3
#           (`bias-rail` only — no delivery at all, NOT a direction anybody may quote)
#     INERT G2 cover 0 of 3, G4 energy 0 of 3
#     60.0 % IS AT THE S1 BOUND WITH NO SLACK, and that is stated rather than smoothed: [MESS] ELEVEN
#     of the 24 levers produce a BIT-IDENTICAL blue trajectory on this rig (`cover` x3, `energy` x3,
#     `net-on`, `sort-left`, `sort-near`, `ccip-open`, `emcon-wide` — the last because with a live net
#     and no threat the seed already radiates continuously, X-14's class), and `bias-early`/`bias-late`
#     move only a bomb whose lattice is centred. Eleven levers can therefore never move this class, so
#     14 of 25 = 56.0 % is the floor this lever file allows and the four ladders reach 60.0 %.
#   RED, 9 levers of tools/levers-red-mig29.txt (the alphabet a MiG-29 can express, E-31): BASELINE
#     (8, 4), 7 distinct classes, modal share 30.0 % (3 of 10), S7 0 of 8 on all 25 (cell, blue) pairs.
#     live  G5 emcon 3 of 5, G3 sort 4 of 4 — 7 movers of 9, 6 of them off their band's rail. Here it
#           is `emcon-lo` and `emcon-hi` that are the identity map and `emcon-tight`/`emcon-mid` that
#           move, the mirror of `sat-10`: this rig briefs 120/90 km and not 120/90/60, so the PUR-31
#           gate `f x 27.0 nm` crosses it at different points.
#
# AND THE CLOCK, because X-7 is the trap: the run duration is 520.0 s on ALL 35 runs of both lever sets
# — one value, no spread at all.
#
# THE ARENA: four F-16 QRA at 6 000..6 450 m against four unarmed An-26 crossing westbound on tracks
# 7.8 km apart, a dry four-ship MiG-29 CAP behind them, and a CCIP pair on two soft aim points.
# `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking (C4). Every coordinate is [SET] except the two aim
# points, which sit at the fixed point of their own release lattice. Day, 11:00 local.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION, ASKED OF BOTH SEATS: WITH NOBODY ABLE TO SHOOT, HOW CLOSE DOES EACH SIDE'S
# SORT ACTUALLY BRING EACH FIGHTER TO THE CONTACT IT WAS NAMED FOR?
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log         `mission WINDOW_CLOSED` at t = 300.1; `mission IDENTIFIED`;
#                      `sms RELEASE_REJECTED` (the dry proof)
#   telemetry_qa*.csv  `flt_src`, `flt_assign`, `flt_switch` — the sort under a 2:1 picture
#
# READING RULE, BINDING: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the ONLY exit this file can produce and is NOT the
# measurement. THE MEASUREMENT IS TWO OUTCOME CLASSES — (V, M) summed over the six F-16 and (V, M)
# summed over the four MiG-29 — AND THE SPREAD OF EACH ACROSS ITS OWN LEVER SET. They are never
# compared with each other. A single run measures NOTHING, and a reader who reports "how many contacts
# were identified" has answered a question this file does not ask.


unit qa1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight qa 1
  spawn 33.20000 43.90000 6000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm sim
  set task intercept
  wp 33.20000 45.10000 6000 480
  objective identify unit mg1 range 4875 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit mg1 range 9247 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit mg1 range 9706 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit mg1 range 9911 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit mg1 range 10115 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective identify unit mg1 range 10422 hold 0.1 until 300
  objective survive until 300

